<title>BRAZIL: Brazil non-ferrous metals - September statistics.</title>
<headline>Brazil non-ferrous metals - September statistics.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production in September 1996 and consumption, imports and exports of Brazilian non-ferrous metals in January/September 1996 compared with 1995 were as follows, said the Secretariat of Mines and Metallurgy.</p>
<p>All figures are in tonnes.</p>
<p> METAL		  PRODUCTION (SEPT)   CONSUMPTION (JAN/SEPT)</p>
<p>			   1996	 1995	    1996	 1995</p>
<p> Aluminium	   97,500     97,800	 474,436    387,421</p>
<p> Lead			 0	1,462	     n/a     55,881</p>
<p> Copper		15,369     15,528	 166,695    158,704</p>
<p> Tin		    1,517	1,672	   4,912	4,463</p>
<p> Magnesium		n/a	  n/a	     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p> Nickel		 1,380	1,249	  14,592     14,168</p>
<p> Zinc		  14,900     16,971	 100,650    142,367</p>
<p> METAL		   EXPORTS (JAN/SEPT)     IMPORTS (JAN/SEPT)</p>
<p>			   1996	 1995	    1996	 1995</p>
<p> Aluminium	  508,278    590,721	  61,450     80,749</p>
<p> Lead		   1,514	2,410	  25,463     43,816</p>
<p> Copper		53,332     43,387     1,070,441    129,252</p>
<p> Tin		    8,296	7,047		51	  158</p>
<p> Magnesium	    1,296	   64	   1,551	2,286</p>
<p> Nickel		 4,375	3,512	   7,187	5,799</p>
<p> Zinc		  40,478     35,097	   5,124     33,540</p>
<p>((-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
